🌐 Custom Domain
I also explored configuring a custom domain for the Microsoft Entra ID tenant.
The default tenant domain was available, but the custom-domain configuration was not successfully completed.
For this lab, the default Microsoft-provided onmicrosoft.com domain is sufficient because a custom domain is not required for the IAM exercises.
DNS Concepts Explored
During the domain configuration process, I learned about:
•	TXT records — used for domain verification. 
•	MX records — used to identify mail servers. 
•	Host/Alias — identifies the DNS name where the record applies. 
•	Destination/Value — contains the record value. 
•	TTL (Time To Live) — controls how long DNS information can be cached.
